@startuml
!include https://raw.githubusercontent.com/proveo-ca/identity/main/proveo.puml
title Monorepo subdir scope — what reaches /app, and what used to be missing

' covers: internal/workspace/mount.go

node "Host repo" as HOST <<host>> {
  component "scope dir\n""apps/web""" as SCOPE <<app>>
  component "root .git" as GIT <<app>>
  component "rootFiles — FILES\nAGENTS.md · package.json · turbo.json …" as RF <<app>>
  component "rootDirs — DIRECTORIES\n""_spec"" · ""vendor""" as RD <<app>>
  component "DepLangs at the repo root\n""node_modules"" · ""target"" · "".venv"" …" as RDD <<app>>
}

node "Container /app" as APP <<host>> {
  component "/app/apps/web  rw" as M1 <<app>>
  component "/app/.git  ro|rw" as M2 <<app>>
  component "/app/<file>  ro" as M3 <<app>>
  component "/app/_spec  rw" as M4 <<app>>
  component "/app/<dep dir>  rw\nprivate copy" as M5 <<app>>
}

component "dotenv mask\n""/dev/null"":ro" as MASK <<app>>
component "host-arch binaries\ncannot exec in the container" as ARCH <<error>>

SCOPE ARROW_MAIN M1
GIT   ARROW_MAIN M2
RF    ARROW_MAIN M3
RD    ARROW_MAIN M4
RDD   ARROW_OPTIONAL M5 : present trees only, plain-copied\n""PROVEO_MOUNT_ROOT_DEPS=0"" omits them
M4    ARROW_QUEUE MASK : walked for secrets
M5    ARROW_ERROR ARCH

note right of RD
  **The gap this closes.** Before ""rootDirs"", a subdir scope mounted the scope
  itself, the root "".git"", and a handful of root FILES — every root DIRECTORY
  except "".git"" and the harness config dir was simply absent. In this fleet
  that hid ""_spec/"" from the agent: the specs it is asked to read and maintain
  were not in the container at all.

  ""rootFiles"" cannot express this. Each entry is bind-mounted as a single file,
  so a directory needs its own list with its own rule.
end note

note bottom of M4
  **Read-write, unlike rootFiles.** ""_spec"" is authored, not merely read — the
  spec-keeper subagent maintains it, and ""plantuml"" is on the floor precisely so
  an agent can verify the artifact it just edited. A dependency tree likewise
  must stay writable or an install inside the container fails against a
  read-only mount.
end note

note bottom of MASK
  **Whole directories must not become a hole in the secret masking.** In
  proxy/firewall mode every dotenv file under the mounted tree is masked with
  ""/dev/null"", the structural complement to the broker header-strip and the
  egress DLP. ""rootFiles"" needs no walk — it is a fixed non-secret allowlist —
  but a vendored package carrying a "".env"" would otherwise be readable here
  while the scope's own is masked. ""node_modules"" is exempt for the reason
  ""envMaskPrune"" already skips it: huge, and never the project's own secrets.
end note

note right of ARCH
  **Never a bind of the host tree.** Each dependency dir
  the table names — at the root here, and under the scope
  at ""/app/<rel>/<dir>"" — is a private plain copy staged
  under the run's state dir. Same OS/arch: the copy is
  reused. Foreign: the seed clears and rebuilds it, host
  untouched. ""_spec/packages/lib/dependency-trees.puml"".
end note

note right of M2
  This is the only branch where "".git"" gets a mount of its own, and the only
  one where ""gitMode"" is consulted — see
  ""_spec/internal/workspace/git-mount-by-scope.puml"".
end note

note bottom of M1
  The scope's own copy always wins: a root directory is mounted only when the
  scope does not already have one by that name, the same union rule ""rootFiles""
  uses, so a repo never sees a path it lacks.
end note
@enduml
